# sunshine-ds (desktop GameStream)

Two servers: Decky Flatpak `:47989` (KMS) and Distrobox sunshine-ds `:48100` (`capture = kwin`). Pin Thor/Odin Moonlight to `:48100`. Dual-stream is Plasma/KWin only.

- `pgrep -x sunshine-ds` only. Never `pgrep -f` / `pkill -f` sunshine. Never put `sunshine-ds-virtual-output` in a `pgrep -f` pattern; kill leftover helpers by numeric PID.
- Exactly one long-lived `sunshine-ds-virtual-output --name sunshine-ds` at 1920×1080 during dual-stream. `--stop` kills it before Game Mode.
- Do not replace Decky Sunshine, `POST /api/restart`, `sudo systemctl --user`, or `kwin_wayland --replace`. Compositor `reinitialize` is last-resort for an all-black KWin FBO (kills the helper).
- Do not use `kscreen-doctor` to decide if `Virtual-sunshine-ds` exists (hangs with duplicates).
- Standalone Flatpak Cemu/Azahar for dual-screen, never RetroDECK `-f`. Cemu type is Wii U GamePad. Azahar is Separate Windows + `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb`. Bind with `scripts/bind-gamepad.py`. Default `GAMESTREAM_PAD_PROFILE=x360`.
- Bring-up: `scripts/ensure-sunshine-ds.sh`. Return to Game Mode: Desktop shortcut or `scripts/switch-to-game-mode.sh`.
- Debug: `.cursor/skills/sunshine-ds-gamestream/SKILL.md`. Stack/SHAs: `.cursor/skills/sunshine-ds-gamestream/reference.md`.
